# Day 3 – Power BI Learning Journey | DAX Practice

Today I learned the basics of DAX (Data Analysis Expressions) in Power BI.  
Practiced creating Measures, Calculated Columns, and commonly used DAX functions for business analytics.

---

# Most Used DAX Formulas

## 1. Aggregate Functions

### SUM
```DAX
Total Sales = SUM(Sales[SalesAmount])
```

### AVERAGE
```DAX
Average Sales = AVERAGE(Sales[SalesAmount])
```

### COUNT
```DAX
Total Orders = COUNT(Sales[OrderID])
```

### DISTINCTCOUNT
```DAX
Unique Customers = DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[CustomerID])
```

---

# 2. Logical Functions

### IF
```DAX
Profit Status =
IF(Sales[Profit] > 0, "Profit", "Loss")
```

### SWITCH
```DAX
Grade =
SWITCH(
    TRUE(),
    Sales[Score] >= 90, "A",
    Sales[Score] >= 70, "B",
    "C"
)
```

---

# 3. Text Functions

### CONCATENATE
```DAX
Full Name =
Employees[FirstName] & " " & Employees[LastName]
```

### UPPER
```DAX
Upper Name = UPPER(Employees[Name])
```

### LOWER
```DAX
Lower Name = LOWER(Employees[Name])
```

---

# 4. Mathematical Functions

### DIVIDE
```DAX
Profit Margin =
DIVIDE(
    SUM(Sales[Profit]),
    SUM(Sales[SalesAmount])
)
```

### ROUND
```DAX
Rounded Sales = ROUND(Sales[SalesAmount], 2)
```

---

# 5. Date & Time Functions

### TODAY
```DAX
Today's Date = TODAY()
```

### YEAR
```DAX
Year = YEAR(Sales[OrderDate])
```

### MONTH
```DAX
Month = MONTH(Sales[OrderDate])
```

---

# 6. Filter Functions

### CALCULATE
```DAX
Total Sales West =
CALCULATE(
    SUM(Sales[SalesAmount]),
    Sales[Region] = "West"
)
```

### FILTER
```DAX
High Sales =
FILTER(
    Sales,
    Sales[SalesAmount] > 1000
)
```

---

# 7. Relationship Functions
### RELATED
```DAX
Product Category =
RELATED(Product[Category])
```

